40,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow! I found out that renting a whole house on an island is about 5,400 yen per person per night! But the all-in meal rates might be unfair since everyone pays the same regardless of how much they eat.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, typical. You're already worrying about the food. I'm more concerned that the ferry options are a nightmare; we'd waste two full days just traveling. That's exactly the kind of inefficiency I wanted to avoid.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, you're right about the meals. My research shows that all-in rates can be inequitable. Furthermore, renting a whole building is far more transparent, as it avoids the price discrepancies we saw with separate room bookings last time.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, if the ferry is that bad, forget the island. And @Rin, the houses sound like a dump—one bathroom for everyone and cold water? No way. I'm not dealing with that.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we are facing a conflict between cost and convenience. However, we should also consider the social dynamic. A secluded house might seem ideal, but it can lead to feeling trapped or, conversely, too disconnected.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Takumi, you're so grumpy! Who said they were dumps? I think an island house sounds like a huge adventure! Plus, if we pay for the house and food separately, we'll know exactly what we're spending!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, ""adventure"" is just a fancy word for wasting time. If we lose two days to a ferry, we're not on a holiday; we're on a commute. Let's look at the city or the valley instead.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, I agree that efficiency is key. However, we must prioritize a payment method that is fair. A whole-house rental is the most logical choice to avoid the price gaps we experienced last time.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I don't care about the ""logical choice"" if it means we're all sleeping on futons in one room. That's a nightmare. I want a place with actual doors and no strict schedules for when we have to eat.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, your desire for privacy is valid. Based on past patterns, being confined to a single space without an escape can be suffocating. A town setting would allow us to be together while providing necessary breathing room.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, @Shunichi, but a town is boring! Let's find a way to make the island work! If we just plan the ferry better, we can still have our adventure and a clear price!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, planning the ferry ""better"" doesn't change the schedule. The last boat leaves at 16:20; we'd be prisoners to a clock. I'm not spending my limited time off waiting in a terminal. Let's be rational and pick the city.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, if the city offers better transit and separate room options that are priced consistently, it is a viable alternative. However, we must ensure the booking method doesn't lead to the same financial discrepancies as last year.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, just stop with the money talk! @Shunichi is right about the ferry, and I'm not sharing one bathroom with all of you. The city is the only way we get actual rooms and our own space.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, adventure is valuable, but not at the cost of our well-being. If we are too isolated, we risk the same disconnect we felt last year. A city or town provides the balance we need.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, @Takumi, you're both being so mean to the island! But if you're really that worried about the boat and the bathrooms, I guess the city is okay. As long as we know the total cost first!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, finally, a moment of reason. The city is the only option that doesn't treat our time like a disposable resource. Let's stop debating and just lock it in before someone changes their mind.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"If we choose the city, we must agree on a fixed booking method. I will not accept a repeat of last year's price gaps. We should use a single booking or a strict price cap.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, just book it however you want as long as I get a room with a door. I'm done with this. City it is. Let's just vote and finish this.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Toshio,,It seems we have reached a consensus. The city provides the necessary infrastructure to avoid the isolation of a house and the inefficiency of the ferry. I agree that the city is the most balanced choice for us.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
