64,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I still think the island would be the most exciting, but I don't want everyone to be grumpy! If the city means we can figure out the total cost clearly, I'm okay with that!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your willingness to compromise is a miracle. The city is the only rational choice here; it saves us from the ferry nightmare and gives us actual freedom. I'm voting for the city.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, I agree. While the island house offered a single bill, the city break is the most practical given the group's constraints. As long as we standardize the room costs, I vote for the city.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, just stop talking about the bills! I'm voting for the city because I'm not sharing a room with everyone or dealing with a strict dinner schedule. It's the only way this trip won't be a disaster.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"The city break offers the most flexibility. It prevents the suffocating feeling of a shared house while avoiding the total fragmentation we experienced last year. For the sake of our group's balance, I vote for the city.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if we go to the city, does that mean we each pay for our own things? I just want to make sure I know the total price before we go! I'll vote for the city!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, yes, that's the point of a city break. You manage your own budget, and we avoid the ""all-in"" traps. It's the most efficient way to handle this. My vote remains the city.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, that is exactly why it is the most equitable option. By managing our own expenses, we eliminate the risk of anyone subsidizing another's costs. I vote for the city.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Rin, just let Asuka handle the math if you're that worried. I'm just glad we're not stuck in some inn with a 6 PM dinner bell. I'm voting for the city.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, @Asuka, the city's structure allows us to be together by choice rather than by obligation. It provides the necessary space to prevent friction. My vote is firmly for the city.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Takumi, I can't just let Asuka do the math, I want to know myself! But since everyone else is so sure, I'm happy to go with the group. City it is! I'm voting for the city!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your obsession with the math is almost as tiring as your love for ""adventure."" But since we've finally reached a consensus without a total meltdown, I'm satisfied. City it is. My vote is C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"The consensus is clear and the logic is sound. By choosing the city, we prioritize both efficiency and financial fairness. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm just glad we're finally done arguing. No shared bathrooms, no strict schedules, and no futons. I'm voting for Option C. Let's just get this booked.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, @Shunichi, @Asuka, @Takumi, it is rare that we agree so quickly. The city provides the ideal balance of togetherness and independence. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Shunichi"",""Asuka"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Rin,,"Yay! We all agree! I'm voting for Option C! I can't wait to see the city and find some cool shops, as long as we keep a list of the costs!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, just keep your list and leave us in peace. I'm voting for Option C. Let's just make sure the booking is handled quickly so we can actually relax.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. To ensure the financial transparency I've emphasized, we should finalize the booking details immediately. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Takumi,,Whatever. I'm voting for Option C. Just make sure we actually get those separate rooms and I'm happy. Let's just finish this already.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The decision is unanimous. Option C provides the necessary space to ensure we remain a cohesive group without feeling crowded. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
